<clickhouse>
    <!-- Disable the heavy, non-diagnostic system.*_log tables entirely, mirroring
         trace_log_disabled.xml. Under a fuzzer-paced workload these tables accumulate parts
         continuously and are pure disk/IO overhead: metric_log / asynchronous_metric_log /
         query_metric_log write periodic metric snapshots every few hundred ms regardless of
         query activity, and the per-query/per-thread/per-view logs multiply with sqlancer's
         high statement rate. sqlancer dev runs never read any of them.

         The `remove="remove"` attribute is the documented ClickHouse mechanism for cancelling a
         parent-config entry from a config.d override: it deletes the <NAME_log> block from
         /etc/clickhouse-server/config.xml so the server never creates the table on startup. This
         skips the writes altogether (heavier hammer than a TTL cap, which still accumulates writes
         between merges). A name that does not exist on the running build is silently ignored, so
         listing a superset is safe across head versions.

         processors_profile_log is moved here from system_log_ttl.xml: a full remove beats the
         former 1-hour TTL (no writes vs capped retention).

         DELIBERATELY KEPT ENABLED (do not add here): query_log is the canonical reproducer-triage
         input (which query failed on which thread); part_log is the merge/part lifecycle log that
         several MergeTree wrong-result bugs (merge-formed parts) are diagnosed from; error_log and
         crash_log are tiny and load-bearing for triage.

         text_log was moved to the removed set (it is recreated only on server start, so dropping it
         at runtime disables it without a restart): the reproducer files (database*.log) already
         carry the failing query + stack, so text_log is redundant for triage and is pure
         disk/IO overhead under the fuzzer-paced statement rate. -->
    <text_log remove="remove"/>
    <metric_log remove="remove"/>
    <asynchronous_metric_log remove="remove"/>
    <query_metric_log remove="remove"/>
    <processors_profile_log remove="remove"/>
    <query_thread_log remove="remove"/>
    <query_views_log remove="remove"/>
    <opentelemetry_span_log remove="remove"/>
    <latency_log remove="remove"/>
    <blob_storage_log remove="remove"/>
    <backup_log remove="remove"/>
</clickhouse>
